:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;7&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;8&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:[{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;5&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0}},{&quot;1&quot;:0,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;3&quot;:3},{&quot;1&quot;:1,&quot;2&quot;:0,&quot;4&quot;:1}]},&quot;9&quot;:1,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:3,&quot;3&quot;:1},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:12,&quot;17&quot;:1}\" data-sheets-formula=\"=SUM(R[-30]C[0]:R[-1]C[0])\">The contractor has submitted for a full refund of the balance retention money, (9.32 million) but at this juncture, we may only refund the remainder of the 50% retention money, (2.13 million).</span></p>\r\n<p>The final bill is being verified, with the work value of Nu. 130 million. The calculated liquidated damages at&nbsp;<strong>0.1</strong><strong>%</strong>&nbsp;of the contract price of 134.44 million, for 53 days works out to Nu. 7.12 million. The budget for the final bill of Nu. 13 million shall be sufficient for the penalty imposed.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for kind review and approval for half the total amount retained to be repaid to the contractor on completion of the whole of the works = Nu. 2,134,915.32</p>',135,'2024-06-18 10:46:03','2024-06-19 09:58:45',8,98),
(23,'2024-06-18',23,1,'Seeking kind approval for release of payment of final invoice from Perfect Builder Store Ltd for supply of roofing materials  ','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Submitted herewith are the following invoice of total&nbsp; amounting to Nu. 19,813.00 (Ngultrum Nineteen Thousand Eight Hundred Thirteen) only, for the supply of roofing materials from Perfect Builder Store Limited, Thimphu&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">1) Invoice No: PBSL/SALE/2024/May/16/18 dated May 01, 2024 = Nu. 3,950.00</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2) Invoice No. PBSL/SALE/2024/May/16/399 date May 10, 2024= Nu. 6,450.00</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">3) Invoice No. PBSL/SALE/2024/Jun/16/436 dated June 10, 2024 = Nu. 7,163.00</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">4) Invoice No. PBSL/SALE/2024/Jun/16/433 dated June 10, 2023 = Nu. 2,250.00</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The cost shall be utilized from the budget head spill over budget &ldquo;HQ roofing and rainwater down pipe\".&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Therefore, seeking kind approval for release of payment as per approved note sheet no. 10030 dated 29/02/2024.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Submitted please.</span></p>',139,'2024-06-18 11:11:26','2024-06-19 10:01:15',8,20),
(24,'2024-06-18',24,1,'Seeking approval for Eastern Region Tour','<p>Internal Audit Unit would like to submit that the following Post offices under eastern Region were not audited for the previous two years and were&nbsp; last audited in First Quarter of 2021. As per the annual work plan 2024, audit and inspection for the majority of PO\'s under Eastern Region shall be covered this time and few PO\'s were provisioned in October -December 2024. In this regard, IAU team proposed to carry out the audit and Inspection of the aforementioned POs as per the tentative programe.</p>\r\n<p>The plan for audit &amp; Inspection is included in approved annual work plan 2024, and scheduled as below.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Sonam Penjor &amp; Kinley Dorji</p>\r\n<p>1. Thimphu to Gyelpoishing- 24-25.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>2. Gyelpoishing to Lhuntse-26.6 2024</p>\r\n<p>3. Lhuntse to Mongar- 27-29.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>4. Mongar to Trashi yangtse 30.6 2024 to 1.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>5. Yangtse to Doksum- 2-3.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>6. Doksum to Trashigang 4-6 7.2024</p>\r\n<p>7. Trashigang to Rangjung 7.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>8. Rangjung to Kanglung 8-9.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>9. Kanglung to Wamrong 10-11.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>10.Wamrong to Pemagatshel 12-13. 7. 2024</p>\r\n<p>11. Pema Gatshel to Mongar 14.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>12. Mongar to Thimphu. 15.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>The&nbsp; start and end&nbsp; dates for the tour have been set in, but it is felt important to maintain flexibility when travelling between stations because we might have to travel in night depending on the state of road. Additionally, the return journey via Bumthang or Pemagatshel via Sjongkhar -Phuntsholing shall be kept open, subject on road conditions.</p>\r\n<p>In line with above tour, the officials also would like to request for DSA adavnce of Nu. 25000.00 please.</p>\r\n<p>Kinley Dorji DSA advance- Nu. 10000.00</p>\r\n<p>Sonam Penjor DSA advance- Nu.15000.00</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, Dasho is kindly requested to approve our 23 days official tour and advance DSA&nbsp; please.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,'2024-06-18 15:15:16','2024-06-18 15:15:16',2,NULL),
(25,'2024-06-18',25,1,'Approval for purchase of UPS equipment.','<p>This is to apprise management that the ICT Division has received requisitions for the purchase of four Uninterruptible Power Supply (UPS) units from the Samtse, Lhamozingkha, Sipsoo, and Nanglam Post Offices (PO).</p>\r\n<p>Recently, these offices have experienced several power outages and fluctuations that have resulted in downtime, data loss, and equipment damage. The current UPS equipment is no longer capable of providing the necessary protection and services. Considering the urgent need and importance of the UPS equipment to ensure the continuous and reliable operation of services, the ICT Division would like to propose and submit for management approval the procurement of four UPS units for the four POs.</p>\r\n<p>The procurement of the UPS equipment will be based on Bhutan Post\'s annual quotation rates and specifications, which are Nu. 6248 per UPS. The budget will be met from the approved capital budget allocated for UPS equipment, amounting to Nu. 0.128 million under the ICT division for the Financial Year 2024.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for your kind approval.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',249,'2024-06-18 15:40:23','2024-06-19 09:59:48',8,908),
(26,'2024-06-18',26,1,'Seeking approval for Eastern Region Tour','<p>Internal Audit Unit would like to submit that the following POs under Eastern Regions were not able to audit for previous two year which were last audited in First quarter of 2021. AS per our annual work plan the majority of the POs under the region shall be covered this time and only for few POs were provisioned in October-December 2024. In this regard, IAU proposed to carry out Audit &amp; Inspection of following POs as per the tentative programe.</p>\r\n<p>The plan for audit &amp; Inspection is included in approved annual plan of IAU, the schedule is as below.</p>\r\n<p>Mr. Sonam Penjor &amp; Mr. Kinley Dorji</p>\r\n<p>Thimphu to&nbsp; Gyelpoishing-&nbsp; 24-25.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Gyelpoishing&nbsp; to Lhuntshi - 26.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Lhuntse to Mongar- 27-29.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar to Trashi Yangtse- 30.6.2024 to 1.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashi Yangtse to Doksum- 2-3.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Doksum to Trashigang- 4-6.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashigang to Rangjung- 7.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Rangjung to Kanglung- 8-9.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Kanglung to Wamrong 10-11.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Wamrong to Pemagatshel- 12-23.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Wamrong to Mongar- 14.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar- Thimphu- 15.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The start and ending dates for the tour have been set in, but it is felt important to maintain flexibility when travelling between stations, as we may need to travel at night depending on the state of roads. Additionally, the return journey via Bumthang or Pemagatshel via Sjongkhar-Phuntsholing shall remain open and optional, subject to road conditions.</p>\r\n<p>Officials also would like to request DSA advance of Nu. 25000.00 to met the expenses during above tour.</p>\r\n<p>1. Sonam Penjor Nu. 15000.00</p>\r\n<p>2. Kinley Dorji&nbsp; Nu. 10000.00</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, Dasho is requested to kindly approve our proposed 23-day official tour and DSA advance please.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,'2024-06-18 15:49:18','2024-06-18 15:49:18',2,NULL),
(27,'2024-06-18',27,1,'Seeking approval for Eastern Region Tour','<p>Internal Audit Unit would like to submit that the following POs under Eastern Regions were last audited in First quarter of year 2021, and unable to conduct audit for the past two year. As per our annual work plan the majority POs of the region will be covered by this tour and remaining Regional Office, GPO Samdrupjongkhar and few Pos shall be covered by our next tour which will take place in October - December 2024. In this regard, IAU would like to propose the Audit &amp; Inspection of following POs as per the tentative programe.</p>\r\n<p>The Plan for the Audit &amp; Inspection is included in approved&nbsp; annual work plan of IAU, and the schedule is as below.</p>\r\n<p>Thimphu to Gyelpoising- 24-25.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Gyelpoishing to Lhuntse- 26.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Lhuntse to Mongar- 27-29.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar to Trashi Yangtse- 30.6.2024 to 1.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashi Yangtse to Doksum - 2-3.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Doksum to Trashigang- 4-6.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashigang to Rangjung- 7.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Rangjung to Kanglunf- 8-9.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Kanglung to Wamrong-10-11.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Wamrong to pemagatshel-12-13.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Pemagatshe to Mongar- 14.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar to Thimphu- 15.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>The start and ending dates for the tour have been determined, but travelling from station to stations need to be flexible, as sometimes we may need to travel at night depending on the states of roads. Additionally, the return journey via Bumthang or Pemagatshel via Sjongkhar-Phuntsholing shall remain open and optional, subjects to road conditions.</p>\r\n<p>To cover the expenses during above tour, the official would like to request for DSA advance of Nu. 25000.00&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Kinley Dorji- Nu.10000.00</p>\r\n<p>Sonam Penjor Nu. 15000.00</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, Dasho is requested to kindly approve the proposed 23 days official tour and the DSA advance please.</p>',NULL,'2024-06-18 16:21:50','2024-06-18 16:21:50',2,142),
(28,'2024-06-18',28,1,'Seeking approval for Eastern Region Tour','<p>Internal Audit Unit would like to submit that the following POs under Eastern Regions were last audited in First quarter of year 2021, and unable to conduct audit for the past two year. As per our annual work plan the majority POs of the region will be covered by this tour and remaining Regional Office, GPO Samdrupjongkhar and few Pos shall be covered by our next tour which will take place in October - December 2024. In this regard, IAU would like to propose the Audit &amp; Inspection of following POs as per the tentative programe.</p>\r\n<p>The Plan for the Audit &amp; Inspection is included in approved&nbsp; annual work plan of IAU, and the schedule is as below.</p>\r\n<p>Thimphu to Gyelpoising- 24-25.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Gyelpoishing to Lhuntse- 26.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Lhuntse to Mongar- 27-29.6.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar to Trashi Yangtse- 30.6.2024 to 1.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashi Yangtse to Doksum - 2-3.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Doksum to Trashigang- 4-6.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Trashigang to Rangjung- 7.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Rangjung to Kanglunf- 8-9.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Kanglung to Wamrong-10-11.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Wamrong to pemagatshel-12-13.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Pemagatshe to Mongar- 14.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>Mongar to Thimphu- 15.7.2024</p>\r\n<p>The start and ending dates for the tour have been determined, but travelling from station to stations need to be flexible, as sometimes we may need to travel at night depending on the states of roads. Additionally, the return journey via Bumthang or Pemagatshel via Sjongkhar-Phuntsholing shall remain open and optional, subjects to road conditions.</p>\r\n<p>To cover the expenses during above tour, the official would like to request for DSA advance of Nu. 25000.00&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Kinley Dorji- Nu.10000.00</p>\r\n<p>Sonam Penjor Nu. 15000.00</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, Dasho is requested to kindly approve the proposed 23 days official tour and the DSA advance please.</p>',160,'2024-06-18 16:23:05','2024-06-18 16:23:05',2,142),
(29,'2024-06-18',29,1,'Trading and Depository Fee for May 2024','<p>This is to submit that the following Trading and Depository Fee were raised by RSEBL for the month of May 2024</p>\r\n<table width=\"637\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan=\"7\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"556\">\r\n<p><strong>Trading &amp; Depository fee for the Month of May 2024</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"81\">\r\n<p><strong>Remarks</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"62\">\r\n<p><strong>SL.NO</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"85\">\r\n<p><strong>Details</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;Buy </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p><strong>Sell</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"99\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;TOTAL VALUE </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"66\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;Fees </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"88\">\r\n<p><strong>Total Trading &amp; Depository fee</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td rowspan=\"5\" width=\"81\">\r\n<p><strong>Attached invoice</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"62\">\r\n<p>1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"85\">\r\n<p>Trading fee</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p>&nbsp; 51,163.00</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p>43,706.00</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"99\">\r\n<p>&nbsp; 5,605,030.87</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"66\">\r\n<p>0.0015</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"88\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 8,407.55</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"62\">\r\n<p>2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"85\">\r\n<p>Depository fee</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p>&nbsp; 51,163.00</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"78\">\r\n<p>43,706.00</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"99\">\r\n<p>&nbsp; 5,605,030.87</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"66\">\r\n<p>0.00025</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"88\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1,401.26</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan=\"6\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"467\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;TOTAL </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"88\">\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 9,808.81 </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, total of Nu. <strong>9,808.81 /-(Nine Thousand Eight Hundred Eight and Chetrum Eight One)</strong> only may be approved to be released to RSEBL.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for kind approval please</p>',148,'2024-06-19 17:00:28','2024-06-21 14:22:09',8,108),
(30,'2024-06-19',30,1,'Seeking approval to reorganize inbound office and partition with aluminum ','<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is to inform management of the need to reorganize the inbound exchange office at Thimphu GPO. As recommended during recent ORE review by APPU experts to restrict the client from entering freely, it is crucial to install an aluminum partition to limit client access to the inbound office and postal mail.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The estimated cost of the aluminum partition is approximately Nu. 50,000.00 (fifty thousand). Spot quotations will be solicited from at least three potential firms, and the work order will be awarded to the lowest bidder. The budget for this project will be utilized from the repair and maintenance kept under Thimphu GPO for 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Submitted for kind approval, please.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;</p>',155,'2024-06-19 09:57:37','2024-06-19 15:16:58',8,24),
(31,'2024-06-20',31,1,'Disposal of Old Furniture, Tyres, Syntax and Old Scooter along with the disposal of old roofing materials ','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is to submit that the Procurement Unit, AHRD would like to propose for the disposal of old furniture, tyres, syntax and Scooter that have been stored at the rear of the office building. These accumulation items not only create an untidy shobby appearance to the visitor but also could not be traced in our asset register as the items were too old to recognize, thus complicating our inventory management.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Therefore,</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">kindly request your approval to proceed with the disposal of the aforementioned items with the disposal of old roofing materials at your earliest convenience. It may also help to generate some revenue la </span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Submittedfor kind approval, please&nbsp;</span></p>',139,'2024-06-20 15:24:14','2024-06-21 14:21:44',8,20),
(32,'2024-06-20',32,1,'Revision of House Rent ','<p>Sir,</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph;\">This is to bring to your attention that the lease agreement between Bhutan Post Gedu and Gedu College of Business Studies for the premises at Gedu PO is due to expire on 1st July 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph;\">The College Management has expressed their interest in renewing the lease from 1st July 2024 onwards, with a proposed revision in accordance with the GCBS housing policy, 2018 which includes a 2% increase in rent. This adjustment would bring the new rent payable to Nu 1434/- (Nu 1406 + Nu 28) per the terms outlined.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph;\">Therefore, we kindly request your approval for the enhancement of the rental payment to Gedu College of Business Studies, Gedu PO, effective from 1st July 2024 to 30th June 2026.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph;\">For your convenience, a copy of the Lease Agreement is attached for your reference.</p>\r\n<p>Thanking You</p>\r\n<p>Best regards,</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Singye Rinzin</p>\r\n<p>Postmaster</p>\r\n<p>Gedu PO</p>',173,'2024-06-20 15:33:04','2024-06-24 14:00:14',8,177),
(33,'2024-06-21',33,1,'Site development works- final Bill','<p>The site development works were awarded to M/s Shekhar construction and have been completed. The summary of the final bill submission is as follows:</p>\r\n<p>1. Total bill claimed: Nu. 564,497.86&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>2. Verified bill amount: Nu. 305,045.86</p>\r\n<p>3. Additional minor roofing work for the entry and exit ramp completed, at rates equivalent to 2022 BSR rates.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for kind approval</p>',135,'2024-06-21 12:32:48','2024-06-21 12:34:53',6,98),
(34,'2024-06-21',34,1,'Seeking kind approval for maintenance of telephone lines','<p>This is to submit that the telephone line in the office of Head, ICTD, POD and IAU has become unserviceable and needs immediate maintenance. We have contacted M/s. Broadway Communication, Changzamtog to carry out the necessary repairs. The attached documents provide the estimate cost for carrying out the maintenance works.</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, we request your kind approval to carry out the work so that the queries and the communication are attended promptly.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted, please.</p>',138,'2024-06-21 14:18:23','2024-06-21 14:32:46',10,36),
(35,'2024-06-21',35,1,'Seeking kind approval for maintenance of telephone lines','<p>This is to submit that the telephone line in the office of Head, ICTD, POD and IAU has become unserviceable and needs immediate maintenance. We have contacted M/s. Broadway Communication, Changzamtog to carry out the necessary repairs.</p>\r\n<p>The estimate cost for carrying out&nbsp;the maintenance works with materials is Nu. 13,420.00 (Nu. Thirteen Thousand Four Hundred Twenty) only. Estimate submitted by the firm is attached herewith for your kind reference.</p>\r\n<p>The cost incurred will be utilized from the budget head \"<strong>Maintenance of office equipment&rsquo;s</strong>\" kept under ICTD for FY 2024.</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, we request your kind approval to carry out the work so that the queries and the communication are attended promptly.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted, please.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',138,'2024-06-21 14:39:16','2024-06-24 13:58:37',8,36),
(36,'2024-06-21',36,1,'Payment for IPS.post supplementary items over 6\'000 category amounting to CHF 267.30 ','<p>This is to submit to the management that Postal Operation Division has received an invoice no. CTP.VFAC-16003 dated 06.03.2024 amounting to CHF 267.30 from UPU for settlement. The total payable in Ngutrum is 25,326.68(Twenty five thousand three hundred twenty six and chetrum sixty eight)only as on 21.06.2024.</p>\r\n<p>The expenditure shall be met from budget head\" PE statutory Fees-IPS.Post/CDS.Post/Post.net mail/PRIME\"kept under POstal Operation Division with approved budget1.450 million and budget balance of 0.687 million.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for kind approval by the management la.</p>',140,'2024-06-21 17:28:07','2024-06-24 13:55:31',8,18),
(37,'2024-06-24',37,1,'Payment to Taiwan Post in settlement with CN52 General Account 2022 -  Q1-2024','<p>This is to submit to the management that the settlement of CN 52 General Account of 2022 - Q1-2024 amounting to SDR 1,364.00 in favor of CHUNGHWA POST CO., LTD as detailed below:</p>\r\n<p>SDR - 1,364.00</p>\r\n<p>While converting into USD</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;1SDR = $ 1.314950 (USD) as of&nbsp; 21st, June 2024</p>\r\n<p>USD = 1,793.59</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, a total SDR of 1,793.59 (One Thousand Seven Hundred Ninety-Three and Cents Five Nine) may only be approved for the payment to CHUHGHWA POST CO., LTD. The budget is provisioned under the IMR unit in the financial year 2023.</p>\r\n<p>The sanctioned net amount in USD may be paid to the above postal administration after deducting the bank charges and handling fee for the draft/cheque. Verified invoice details are attached herewith for your kind reference and submitted for management\'s kind approval.</p>',NULL,'2024-06-24 10:57:48','2024-06-24 10:57:48',2,NULL),
(38,'2024-06-24',38,1,'Payment to Taiwan Post in settlement with CN52 General Account 2022 -  Q1-2024','<p>This is to submit to the management that the settlement of CN 52 General Account of 2022 - Q1-2024&nbsp; amounting to SDR 1,364.00 in favour of CHUNGHWA POST CO., LTD as detailed below:</p>\r\n<p>SDR - 1,364.00</p>\r\n<p>While converting into USD</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;1SDR = $ 1.314950(USD) as of 21st June 2024</p>\r\n<p>USD = 1,793.59</p>\r\n<p>Therefore, a total SDR of 1,793.59 (One Thousand Seven Hundred Ninety-Three and Cents Five Nine) only, May be approved for the payment to CHUNGHWA POST CO., LTD. The budget is provisioned under the IMR unit in the financial year 2023.</p>\r\n<p>The sanctioned net amount in USD may be paid to the above postal administration after deducting the bank charges and handling fee for the draft/cheque. Verified invoice details are attached herewith for your kind reference and submitted for management\'s kind approval.</p>',156,'2024-06-24 11:07:58','2024-06-25 10:08:23',8,96),
(39,'2024-06-24',39,1,'Renewal of Agreement','<p>Changmari Bakery, located at Norbugang(Changmari) expresses its intention to renew the house rent agreement for the property currently occupied. The existing tenancy agreement is set to expire on 30th July 2024</p>\r\n<p>The Bakery has consistently met all rental obligations and maintained the property in good condition. The current agreement is nearing its end, necessitating discussions on renewal to ensure continued occupancy.</p>\r\n<p>Changmari Bakery wishes to continue as tenants beyond the current lease expiration date of 30th July 2024 has been renewed on dt 24.06.2024 with a 10% increase as Tenancy Act of Bhutan.</p>\r\n<p>We look forward to your consideration of our request for lease renewal the new agreement is attached for your reference.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thanking You</p>\r\n<p>San Bdr Gurung(Postmaster)</p>\r\n<p>Samtse PO.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',NULL,'2024-06-24 12:38:23','2024-06-24 12:38:23',2,NULL),
(40,'2024-06-24',40,1,'Renewal of Agreement','<p>Renewal of House Rent Agreement</p>\r\n<p>Changmari Bakery, the tenant occupying the property located at Norbugang(Changmari) has been renting the premises since 1<sup>st</sup> July 2018. The current renting agreement is set to expire on 30<sup>th</sup> July 2024.</p>\r\n<p>The tenant has expressed their desire to continue renting the property beyond the current lease expiry date. They have been consistent with rent payments and have maintained the property well.</p>\r\n<p>Changmari Bakery formally requests the renewal of the house rent agreement under the same terms and conditions as per the request we have drawn the rental agreement as per Tenancy Act of Bhutan with 10% increase as pert the act.</p>\r\n<p>An inspection of the property before finalizing the renewal is in good condition and maintenance was done on time.</p>\r\n<p>House Rent Agreement is attached for your reference and necessary records.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thank YouThe&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>San Bdr Gurung(Postmaster)</p>\r\n<p>Bhutan Post</p>\r\n<p>Samtse.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>',167,'2024-06-24 14:17:59','2024-06-25 10:55:27',10,172),
(41,'2024-06-24',41,1,'Seeking bill payment approval for printer for printing of UN joint issue peacekeeping stamps.','<p>This is submit to Management that, Brebner prinnter ,NewZealand has submitted the invoice for printing of UN peacekeeing joint issue for USD 4119/-(USD Four Thousand One Hundred Nine) only. Details are as below:</p>\r\n<p>1.Sheetlet-5000 Nos.</p>\r\n<p>2.Sovvenirsheet-5000 Nos.</p>\r\n<p>3.Invoice attached here with.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for approval please.</p>',157,'2024-06-24 14:20:41','2024-06-24 15:44:03',10,138),
(42,'2024-06-24',42,1,'Seeking bill payment approval for printer for printing of UN joint issue peacekeeping stamps.','<p>This is submit to Management that, Brebner printer, New Zealand has raised a invoice amounting USD 4,119/-(Four Thousand One Hundred Nineteen) only for the printing charges for UN peacekeeping joint issue stamps.</p>\r\n<p>Details are as below:</p>\r\n<p>1.Sheetlet-5000 Nos.</p>\r\n<p>2.Souveniershhet-5000 Nos.</p>\r\n<p>3.Invoice attached herewith</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for approval please.</p>',157,'2024-06-24 16:02:14','2024-06-25 10:10:53',8,138),
(43,'2024-06-24',43,1,'Time Extension for 4 months','<p>Extension of Rental Agreement for Yoeseltse(Ghumuney) Tenant</p>\r\n<p>As per the Tenant, from Yoeseltse(Ghumuney) has requested for time extension. The tenant has been residing in our building with an agreement for 4 months starting from 1<sup>st</sup> Feb 2024 and expires on 30<sup>th</sup> May 2024 to complete the construction of their building, which is currently underway. Tenant (Kinzang Norbu) wants additional time to finish the construction of their building.</p>\r\n<p>I would like to seek the approvals for time extension for 4 months, The rent for the extension period will be as per the existing rental agreement.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thank You</p>\r\n<p>San Bdr Gurung(Postmaster)</p>\r\n<p>Bhutan Post</p>\r\n<p>Samtse</p>',167,'2024-06-24 16:03:02','2024-06-25 11:10:50',10,172),
(44,'2024-06-24',44,1,'Seeking kind approval for contribution','<p>This is in line with the invitation received from Tang Rimpochhe to participate in the Good fortune &amp; Prosperity accumulation Prayers at the National Memorial Chorten, Thimphu.</p>\r\n<p>As a token of our support for the significant offerings, Bhutan Post is pleased to express our commitment to contribute a sum of Nu. 25,000.00 (Nu. Twenty Five Thousand) only towards the event.</p>\r\n<p>The budget shall be utilized from the budget head <strong>&ldquo;Staff Welfare-Prayer/Ritual Expenses (Rimdo)&rdquo;</strong> kept under AHRD for FY 2024.</p>\r\n<p>Submitted for kind approval, please.</p>',138,'2024-06-24 16:57:30','2024-06-25 10:09:21',8,36),
(45,'2024-06-24',45,1,'Approval for 90% Daily Allowance for Dasho Chairman Mr. Phuntsho Tobgay & Payment of Air Ticket','<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Universal Postal Union (UPU) has sent an invitation to the Ministry of Infrastructure and Transport(MoIT)t, specifically addressed to the Hon\'ble Secretary, regarding the POC Standing Group Session/Meeting scheduled to take place from 1 July to 5 July 2024 in Bern, Switzerland.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Dasho Chairman has instructed Bhutan Post to provide funding for attending the POC Standing Group Session, and this request has been approved by Bhutan Post as per their letter reference number BP(C)/05/MD/CEO/2024-633 dated June 19, 2024, which was addressed to the officiating Chief HR Officer at MOIT. The funding is intended for the Dasho Chairman to participate in the POC Standing Group Session.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The table below presents the details of the 90% Daily Allowance entitled to the attend&nbsp; the POC Standing Group Session in Bern, Switzerland from 1 July to 5 July 2024:</span></p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td colspan=\"8\">\r\n<p><strong>Daily Allowance Details for Hon\'ble Dasho Chairman</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://sl.no/\"><strong>Sl.No</strong></a></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>From</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>To</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>DATE</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>No.of Days</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>In USD</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>In Nu.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><strong>Halt</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">1</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Paro</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bangkok</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\